#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096419 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8b9014e-32cf-5f04-856c-7fd663bea50f" :question/math-academy-id "e-528" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f'(x) - 3\\sin(2x) = 0$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 3\\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int f^{\\prime }(x)dx &= \\int 3\\sin 2xdx \\\\\nf(x) &= 3\\int \\sin 2xdx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cos 2x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096420 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8e6c58c-da62-5dab-8325-a53c14d9b8ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-529" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2} = x$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}dx &= \\int xdx \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{1}{2}x^{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= \\int (\\frac{1}{2}x^{2} + C)dx \\\\\ny &= \\frac{1}{6}x^{3} + Cx + D\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D$. We cannot combine them, because $C$ is being multiplied by $x$ while $D$ is not."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096421 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab40a4d3-c418-5b64-a04c-bb017155a4d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-530" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $y' = 2x$, and sketch the solution curves of this equation." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C$. The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/3665168b0c99cbb50812c142637a625a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29a0265e-ad88-5ac9-88fe-878aa4f0d0bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-531" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2$.\n$f'(x) - \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2} = 0$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int f^{\\prime }(x)dx &= \\int \\frac{3}{1 + x^{2}}dx \\\\\nf(x) &= 3\\int \\frac{1}{1 + x^{2}}dx \\\\\n&= 3\\arctan x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is\n\n$$\nf(x) = 3\\arctan{x} + C\n$$\n\nTo find a particular solution, we substitute the condition\n\n$$\nf(0) = 2\n$$\n\ninto our solution and obtain a value for $C$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= 3\\arctan (x) + C \\\\\n2 &= 3\\arctan (0) + C \\\\\n2 &= 0 + C \\\\\nC &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\arctan x + 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991a4d75-b082-5ddb-9e0e-daec82c04821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095672} {:answer/id #uuid "b018b6ae-1940-5995-bcd3-0cb355cdfdbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-4e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095673} {:answer/id #uuid "c2357d5d-526c-504c-b3d2-09cc85042828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095674} {:answer/id #uuid "eed6b0a7-f89a-5f99-8fa6-663cdc54a4e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095675} {:answer/id #uuid "5a53ae9e-07c4-5848-85e2-a1c6b214ea93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "991a4d75-b082-5ddb-9e0e-daec82c04821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095672} :answer-field/id #uuid "144fd343-32aa-51c0-ba1c-2d78f454b0d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb82aa2f-3e4a-523a-94c2-c95aa3cb8ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-50136" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} + 4e^{2x} =-2x$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Isolate the derivative: $y'=-2x-4e^{2x}$. Integrating term by term gives\n$$y=-x^2-2e^{2x}+C.$$\nDifferentiation recovers $-2x-4e^{2x}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89aee0c2-41c4-50d9-95e7-d07999f8e43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095678} {:answer/id #uuid "a8264bab-88eb-5c1b-8cf6-4b5658e50c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Cx^{2} + 10x + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095679} {:answer/id #uuid "c8066636-9a63-5ade-85aa-07f7e0be5cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095680} {:answer/id #uuid "0a099fae-b25d-5abb-a50a-c5dc1eda7e34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095681} {:answer/id #uuid "1a40f9c2-33a9-5233-bec8-c51acd272979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8066636-9a63-5ade-85aa-07f7e0be5cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095680} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c860608-75a8-5451-a1a7-a0683cdbc84f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17751a3b-ed4b-5966-a450-330460c02715" :question/math-academy-id "q-50139" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} =-10$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrate twice, introducing a constant at each integration:\n$$y'=-10x+C,\\qquad y=-5x^2+Cx+D.$$\nThe two constants cannot be combined because one multiplies $x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87248665-cb5c-5039-a61b-f40377bba96f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095696} {:answer/id #uuid "ca53b3f7-7fae-554a-ae0b-ae63a12f5e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095697} {:answer/id #uuid "e65a9044-67d3-586d-be0f-d72ddf67972d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095698} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdad7c2-d1f6-5540-909f-d9988ae726bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095699} {:answer/id #uuid "5e919e55-cc7c-5065-9aea-29667e6de4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cdad7c2-d1f6-5540-909f-d9988ae726bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095699} :answer-field/id #uuid "71784ece-a52d-5f27-a140-7ccee85a3e0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27b042e7-c453-5f49-bac9-de5985bbacde" :question/math-academy-id "q-50196" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} =-3(x + 1)^{2}$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrate $y'=-3(x+1)^2$:\n$$y=-(x+1)^3+C.$$\nThese are vertical translations of a decreasing cubic with a horizontal inflection point at $x=-1$. Select the diagram whose decreasing cubic curves flatten at $x=-1$."}]}
